<title>JAPAN: Meiji Life to invest Y300-400 bln in foreign bonds.</title>
<headline>Meiji Life to invest Y300-400 bln in foreign bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meiji Life Insurance Co plans 300 to 400 billion yen worth of fresh investment in foreign bonds in fiscal 1997/98, which started on April 1, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official also said the company plans 200 billion yen of new investment in domestic bonds in the same period.</p>
</text>
